/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  thermoPhysPropDict (v2) -- the apalutamide tablet plant.

  THE FLUIDS.  acetone (the spray-drying solvent -- an ASSUMPTION, see the
  README: no source read confirms the reference product's solvent), nitrogen
  (the inert drying gas of the closed loop and the bulk of the coating air),
  oxygen (the rest of the coating air) and water (the coating suspension's
  carrier and the humidity of the coating air).  An IDEAL liquid (Raoult) and
  an IDEAL gas: the only vapour-liquid question this plant asks is how much
  acetone the -10 C condenser leaves in the nitrogen, and Raoult on an almost
  pure acetone condensate is the right first answer.  N2 and O2 are far above
  their critical temperatures; their extrapolated vapour pressures keep them
  in the gas, and the condensate carries a trace of them.

  THE SOLIDS.  The API, the polymer and every excipient are `role
  nonvolatile;` case-local records in constant/components/: they never enter
  the vapour, they carry no vapour pressure and no critical constants, and
  every stream carries them in its SOLID phase.  NOTHING DISSOLVES in this
  model: the API and the HPMCAS are carried as solids through the solution
  tank into the spray dryer (which reads dissolved and suspended solids
  alike), and so are the PVA and the PEG of the coating suspension.  The heat
  of solution is therefore neglected, and the README says so.

  TRANSPORT.  The spray dryer's drying kinetics need the gas viscosity
  (Chung), conductivity (Eucken) and the solvent's diffusivity in the gas
  (Fuller), computed from the components' own records over the GAS species
  only.  The atomisation reads the liquid's surface tension from the property
  layer: Brock-Bird on the volatile solvent at the feed temperature (a
  corresponding-states estimate; acetone is not hydrogen-bonded, the case in
  which Brock-Bird does best).  The liquid viscosity is NOT a model here: the
  spray solution is a polymer solution whose viscosity no record carries, so
  the dryer's `operation` DECLARES it (system/flowsheetDict).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

recordType    thermophysicalPropertySystem;
schemaVersion 2;

components
(
    acetone  N2  O2  water
    apalutamide  hpmcas
    microcrystallineCellulose  silicifiedMCC  croscarmelloseSodium
    colloidalSilica  magnesiumStearate
    polyvinylAlcohol  polyethyleneGlycol  talcPowder  titaniumDioxide  ironOxide
);

equilibrium
{
    formulation gammaPhi;

    liquid
    {
        activityModel ideal;            // gamma = 1 (Raoult)
        standardState pureLiquid;
    }

    vapour
    {
        fugacityModel idealGas;
    }
}

transport
{
    vapour
    {
        viscosity           { model Chung; }    // gas mu (drying h, k_c)
        thermalConductivity { model Eucken; }   // gas k
        diffusivity         { model Fuller; }   // solvent in the gas
    }

    interface
    {
        surfaceTension { model BrockBird; }     // sigma(T) of the solvent
    }
}

